id: SCA-035
title: Risky pip extra-index-url dependency confusion risk
category: supply-chain
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: requirements.txt Dockerfile Makefile pip.conf
  extensions: .sh .cfg
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
  content_contains: extra-index-url
patterns:
  - regex: --extra-index-url
    message: extra-index-url checks BOTH PyPI and the extra URL. An attacker publishes a same-named package with higher version on PyPI, which pip prefers (dependency confusion).
fix: Use --index-url (replaces default) instead of --extra-index-url (adds to default). Better — use a repository proxy that mirrors PyPI and your private packages.
